1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:04,490
Tokenized stocks can
trade around the clock.

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:09,890
Their underlying markets, and the
liquidity you would need to exit, do not.

3
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:15,650
Kerb is the market-time risk layer
for tokenized stocks on X Layer.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,690
The Board shows that mismatch, live.

5
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:24,330
Each asset keeps its own market
clock, its own liquidity regime,

6
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:26,890
and its own executable capacity.

7
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:30,940
Kerb measures what the real X
Layer pool can absorb right now,

8
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:33,550
and posts it on X Layer mainnet.

9
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:39,830
To measure an exit, Kerb walks the
Uniswap V3 liquidity tick by tick,

10
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:44,610
and finds the largest sale that
clears within 1% price impact.

11
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:47,070
That is C(1%).

12
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:49,950
It cross-checks the answer
against OKX DEX quotes,

13
00:00:49,990 --> 00:00:52,420
and keeps the more conservative number.

14
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:57,210
The Kerb Terms Standard then
binds that capacity to time.

15
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:01,820
Carry is sized to survive the weak
hours until the next deep session,

16
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:03,690
with no action from the borrower.

17
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:09,110
Session Max lends more now, because
it only has to last until Last Call.

18
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:12,190
Either way, the liquidation
line stays fixed.

19
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:15,930
Here, a borrower chooses Session Max.

20
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:20,330
Before anything is signed, Kerb
shows the loan to value, the health,

21
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:24,450
the fixed liquidation line, and
when the next Last Call opens.

22
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:27,570
The loan confirms on X Layer testnet.

23
00:01:33,317 --> 00:01:35,487
Now the clock reaches Last Call.

24
00:01:37,187 --> 00:01:41,657
On testnet, a compressed demo
clock runs this cycle every hour.

25
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:46,550
A Session Max position that borrowed
above its Carry target becomes curable.

26
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:48,550
Only the excess is due.

27
00:01:48,850 --> 00:01:52,540
Any other wallet can repay
it, and earn the cure bonus.

28
00:01:55,217 --> 00:02:00,007
The cure confirms on X Layer, and the
position is back at its Carry target.

29
00:02:00,337 --> 00:02:01,787
This is not a liquidation.

30
00:02:02,037 --> 00:02:03,967
The liquidation line never moved.

31
00:02:05,317 --> 00:02:08,397
Every Kerb term is
posted on X Layer mainnet

32
00:02:08,437 --> 00:02:11,527
with the hash of the
inputs that produced it.

33
00:02:11,657 --> 00:02:14,987
Anyone can fetch those inputs
and recompute the terms.

34
00:02:15,337 --> 00:02:19,107
The Proof page shows the latest
check matching, field by field,

35
00:02:19,317 --> 00:02:22,567
and recent posts carry
the Kerb Builder Code.

36
00:02:23,667 --> 00:02:28,117
Kerb Terms are not tied to Kerb Credit,
which is only the reference consumer.

37
00:02:28,487 --> 00:02:31,257
Agents can buy a credit check over x402.

38
00:02:32,467 --> 00:02:35,617
Contracts on X Layer can
read KerbQuote directly.

39
00:02:36,587 --> 00:02:40,857
Developers can use the
public API, the SDK, or MCP.

40
00:02:41,957 --> 00:02:44,707
Kerb has already measured
why this matters.

41
00:02:45,357 --> 00:02:51,467
When the X Liquidity campaign ended, C(1%)
held at the moment incentives stopped.

42
00:02:51,857 --> 00:02:55,317
A day later, it had fallen 10%
or more for 6 of 10 assets,

43
00:02:55,357 --> 00:02:57,607
and risen for the other four.

44
00:02:58,217 --> 00:02:59,927
Kerb measured that change.

45
00:03:00,357 --> 00:03:01,747
It did not predict it.

46
00:03:02,897 --> 00:03:05,867
The risk plane is live on X Layer mainnet.

47
00:03:06,437 --> 00:03:09,787
Kerb Credit is a testnet reference
market with mirror collateral,

48
00:03:09,957 --> 00:03:11,927
and the contracts are unaudited.

49
00:03:12,577 --> 00:03:15,147
Most systems ask what an asset is worth.

50
00:03:15,797 --> 00:03:18,927
Kerb also asks whether the
exit will still be there.

51
00:03:20,377 --> 00:03:22,467
Never lend more than you can liquidate.

